* Transmission Gate (TG) Comprehensive 9-State Testbench (5V0)

.include "$PDK_ROOT/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/design.ngspice"
.lib "$PDK_ROOT/gf180mcuD/libs.tech/ngspice/sm141064.ngspice" typical

* Include the flattened Magic-extracted netlist
.include "5v0_tg_sc_v2.spice"

* --- Power Supply and Wells ---
* Using the explicit flattened hierarchical node names from the netlist
Vdd gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/VDD 0 DC 5.0
Vss gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/VSS 0 DC 0.0
* Tie the N-Well explicitly to 5V to prevent forward-biasing the PFET bulk
Vnw gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/VNW 0 DC 5.0

* --- Input Stimulus ---
* Signal I (Control Gate): Steps through 0V, 2.5V, and 5.0V every 30ns
V_I gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/I 0 PWL(
+   0.0n  0.0
+  29.8n  0.0
+  30.0n  2.5
+  59.8n  2.5
+  60.0n  5.0
+  90.0n  5.0
+ )

* Signal In (Transmission Source): Cycles 0V, 2.5V, 5.0V every 10ns within each control state
V_In In 0 PWL(
+   0.0n  0.0
+   9.8n  0.0
+  10.0n  2.5
+  19.8n  2.5
+  20.0n  5.0
+  29.8n  5.0
+  30.0n  0.0
+  39.8n  0.0
+  40.0n  2.5
+  49.8n  2.5
+  50.0n  5.0
+  59.8n  5.0
+  60.0n  0.0
+  69.8n  0.0
+  70.0n  2.5
+  79.8n  2.5
+  80.0n  5.0
+  90.0n  5.0
+ )

* --- Loads ---
* Adding realistic 10fF loads to prevent instantaneous non-physical switching 
* and to observe High-Z floating drift on the TG output
C_out out 0 10ff

* --- Simulation Commands ---
.tran 10p 180n
.op

.control
run

* Plot 1: Input Control vs Inverter Output (ZN)
plot v(gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/I) v(gf180mcu_fd_sc_mcu7t5v0__inv_1_0/ZN)

* Plot 2: Transmission Input (In) vs Transmission Output (out)
plot v(In) v(out)

* Plot 3: Current draw to observe crowbar states in the inverter and TG
plot i(Vdd)
.endc
.end